.TH MNN 1 "2026-11-03" "mnn" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mnn \- update installed package managers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mnn
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " [TARGET...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mnn
detects package managers on the host and runs their update commands from a
regular user session. System package managers use a trusted executable path
and refresh
.BR sudo
credentials before execution. Python packages are checked with
.BR "python -m pip list --outdated"
and upgraded individually. Logs are written to the user's state directory.
.SH TARGETS
.B auto
detects installed managers;
.B all
selects all known targets.
Supported targets include apt, apk, AUR helpers, brew, bun, choco, determinate,
dnf, emerge, eopkg, flatpak, pacman, pip, pkg, pnpm, rpm-ostree, snap, soar,
transactional-update, uv, winget, xbps, yum, and zypper.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -n ", " --dry-run
Print planned commands without running package-manager operations.
.TP
.BR -s ", " --silent
Hide package-manager output.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --verbose
Print command details and package-manager output.
.TP
.B --parallel
Run user-level targets concurrently while serializing system targets.
.TP
.B --install-completions [MODE]
Install bash, fish, zsh, or Nushell completions. MODE may be a shell name,
.BR all ,
or
.BR detect .
.TP
.BR -i ", " --install
Install the current executable, manual page, completions, and default config.
.TP
.BR -r ", " --reinstall
Replace the installed executable and selected completions.
.TP
.BR -u ", " --update
Update the installed executable and selected completions when changed.
.TP
.BR -x ", " --uninstall
Remove the executable, manual page, and completions.
.TP
.BR -p ", " --purge
Also remove the config and log files.
.TP
.BR -c ", " --gen-config
Create the default config file.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is
.IR ~/.config/mnn/config .
It accepts
.BR targets ,
.BR verbose ,
.BR silent ,
.BR parallel ,
and
.BR disable-log
settings in
.IR key=value
form.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for configuration and Nushell completion.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for manual page and bash, fish, and zsh completion.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for logs and the run lock.
.TP
.B MNN_SOURCE_DIR
Optional directory containing the binary to install or update.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pip (1),
.BR winget (1),
.BR choco (1)
